      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`TECH-CONTRACT-005` UX/LookDev may continue work after submitting a CONTRACT_REQUEST by creating a `PROVISIONAL_MOCK` outside the canonical Game Contract.",
      "tags": [
        "tech"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "02_PRODUCT_TECH_REQUIREMENTS.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "TECH-CONTRACT-006",
      "domain": "TECH",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`TECH-CONTRACT-006` Every provisional mock must cite its Contract Request ID, mark all unapproved fields as provisional, and state the fallback behavior if Engineering rejects or changes the request.",
      "tags": [
        "tech"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "02_PRODUCT_TECH_REQUIREMENTS.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "TECH-CONTRACT-007",
      "domain": "TECH",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`TECH-CONTRACT-007` Provisional mocks never become authoritative merely because components were built against them.",
      "tags": [
        "tech"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "02_PRODUCT_TECH_REQUIREMENTS.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "TECH-CONTRACT-008",
      "domain": "TECH",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`TECH-CONTRACT-008` When the canonical contract resolves the request, dependent mocks/fixtures must be reconciled or invalidated before implementation is considered complete.",
      "tags": [
        "tech"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "02_PRODUCT_TECH_REQUIREMENTS.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "TECH-OBS-001",
      "domain": "TECH",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`TECH-OBS-001` Maintain an append-only authoritative match event log with stable event IDs, sequence numbers, server timestamps, actor, command/request correlation where relevant, and rule/requirement references where practical.",
      "tags": [
        "tech"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "02_PRODUCT_TECH_REQUIREMENTS.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "TECH-OBS-002",
      "domain": "TECH",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`TECH-OBS-002` Support deterministic match replay/debug reconstruction from initial state + canonical config + authoritative commands/events + RNG provenance.",
      "tags": [
        "tech"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "02_PRODUCT_TECH_REQUIREMENTS.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "TECH-OBS-003",
      "domain": "TECH",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`TECH-OBS-003` Presentation logs and gameplay logs are derived views and are not substitutes for the authoritative event record.",
      "tags": [
        "tech"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "02_PRODUCT_TECH_REQUIREMENTS.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "TECH-CMD-001",
      "domain": "TECH",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`TECH-CMD-001` Critical client commands use explicit request IDs/idempotency keys.",
      "tags": [
        "tech"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "02_PRODUCT_TECH_REQUIREMENTS.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "TECH-CMD-002",
      "domain": "TECH",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`TECH-CMD-002` Duplicate delivery of the same command must not duplicate gameplay effects.",
      "tags": [
        "tech"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "02_PRODUCT_TECH_REQUIREMENTS.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "TECH-CMD-003",
      "domain": "TECH",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`TECH-CMD-003` Draft purchase commands must return an authoritative acknowledgement referencing the request ID and resulting Wallet/supply state.",
      "tags": [
        "tech"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "02_PRODUCT_TECH_REQUIREMENTS.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "TECH-AGENT-001",
      "domain": "TECH",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`TECH-AGENT-001` Use the current OpenAI Agents SDK for TypeScript, not the deprecated experimental OpenAI Swarm project.",
      "tags": [
        "tech"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "02_PRODUCT_TECH_REQUIREMENTS.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "TECH-AGENT-002",
      "domain": "TECH",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`TECH-AGENT-002` Core planning uses manager-style orchestration. Astra remains the conversation owner and invokes specialists as agent tools where appropriate.",
      "tags": [
        "tech"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "02_PRODUCT_TECH_REQUIREMENTS.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "TECH-AGENT-003",
      "domain": "TECH",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`TECH-AGENT-003` Specialists cannot recursively spawn arbitrary specialists.",
      "tags": [
        "tech"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "02_PRODUCT_TECH_REQUIREMENTS.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "TECH-AGENT-004",
      "domain": "TECH",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`TECH-AGENT-004` Deterministic workflow transitions belong in application code when judgment is unnecessary.",
      "tags": [
        "tech"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "02_PRODUCT_TECH_REQUIREMENTS.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "TECH-AGENT-005",
      "domain": "TECH",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`TECH-AGENT-005` Planning agents receive no production filesystem mutation, shell, deployment, Git commit/push, billing, or destructive tools.",
      "tags": [
        "tech"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "02_PRODUCT_TECH_REQUIREMENTS.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "TECH-AGENT-006",
      "domain": "TECH",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`TECH-AGENT-006` Execution agents may receive sandbox-scoped tools only through approved WorkPackages.",
      "tags": [
        "tech"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "02_PRODUCT_TECH_REQUIREMENTS.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "TECH-AGENT-007",
      "domain": "TECH",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`TECH-AGENT-007` Structured outputs use Zod or another SDK-supported schema and are revalidated by application code at authority boundaries.",
      "tags": [
        "tech"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "02_PRODUCT_TECH_REQUIREMENTS.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "TECH-AGENT-008",
      "domain": "TECH",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`TECH-AGENT-008` Built-in SDK tracing remains enabled by default unless explicitly disabled for an operational/privacy reason.",
      "tags": [
        "tech"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "02_PRODUCT_TECH_REQUIREMENTS.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "TECH-AGENT-009",
      "domain": "TECH",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`TECH-AGENT-009` Local run manifests record only usage metrics actually exposed by the SDK. Never fabricate per-agent token attribution.",
      "tags": [
        "tech"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "02_PRODUCT_TECH_REQUIREMENTS.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "TECH-AGENT-010",
      "domain": "TECH",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`TECH-AGENT-010` SDK `maxTurns` and application-level RunBudget are both required.",
      "tags": [
        "tech"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "02_PRODUCT_TECH_REQUIREMENTS.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "TECH-AGENT-011",
      "domain": "TECH",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`TECH-AGENT-011` SDK approval/interruption mechanisms should be used for approval-gated tools where appropriate, while application governance determines whether approval is required.",
      "tags": [
        "tech"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "02_PRODUCT_TECH_REQUIREMENTS.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "TECH-AGENT-012",
      "domain": "TECH",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`TECH-AGENT-012` Sandbox Agents are gated execution infrastructure, not default planning infrastructure.",
      "tags": [
        "tech"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "02_PRODUCT_TECH_REQUIREMENTS.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "TECH-AGENT-013",
      "domain": "TECH",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`TECH-AGENT-013` Model IDs and optional model settings are centralized and environment-overridable.",
      "tags": [
        "tech"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "02_PRODUCT_TECH_REQUIREMENTS.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "TECH-AGENT-014",
      "domain": "TECH",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`TECH-AGENT-014` Astra fallback is explicit and logged. Never silently replace Astra.",
      "tags": [
        "tech"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "02_PRODUCT_TECH_REQUIREMENTS.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "TECH-AGENT-015",
      "domain": "TECH",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`TECH-AGENT-015` Canonical context is retrieved by relevant IDs/slices rather than injected wholesale into every specialist call.",
      "tags": [
        "tech"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "02_PRODUCT_TECH_REQUIREMENTS.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "CONTRACT-001",
      "domain": "CONTRACT",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`CONTRACT-001` Outcome-affecting values come from authoritative state.",
      "tags": [
        "contract"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "03_GAME_CONTRACT.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "CONTRACT-002",
      "domain": "CONTRACT",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`CONTRACT-002` Presentation may own hover, animation progress, interpolation, camera, shader intensity, and temporary emphasis.",
      "tags": [
        "contract"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "03_GAME_CONTRACT.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "CONTRACT-003",
      "domain": "CONTRACT",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`CONTRACT-003` Client presentation never becomes a second rules engine.",
      "tags": [
        "contract"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "03_GAME_CONTRACT.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "CONTRACT-004",
      "domain": "CONTRACT",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`CONTRACT-004` Missing authoritative information requires `CONTRACT_REQUEST`.",
      "tags": [
        "contract"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "03_GAME_CONTRACT.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "CONTRACT-005",
      "domain": "CONTRACT",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`CONTRACT-005` UX/LookDev may use a separately marked `PROVISIONAL_MOCK` while a request is pending.",
      "tags": [
        "contract"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "03_GAME_CONTRACT.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "CONTRACT-006",
      "domain": "CONTRACT",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`CONTRACT-006` Provisional mocks never gain canonical authority by usage.",
      "tags": [
        "contract"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "03_GAME_CONTRACT.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "CONTRACT-007",
      "domain": "CONTRACT",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`CONTRACT-007` Contract versions are explicit and fixtures declare which version they target.",
      "tags": [
        "contract"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "03_GAME_CONTRACT.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "CONTRACT-008",
      "domain": "CONTRACT",
      "status": "current",
      "version": "2.0.0",
      "text": "`CONTRACT-008` Node Power is an alias for Node P1 Power and Node P2 Power. Do not add a redundant `node_power` field for UI convenience.",
      "tags": [
        "contract"
      ],
      "supersedes": [],
      "superseded_by": [],
      "document": "03_GAME_CONTRACT.md"
    }
  ]
